            <profile id="5872-5068-4e74-6214" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="b792-78e1-7b03-d4d6" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Armed with a hand weapon, light armour, thrusting spear and bow. May have a throwing spear instead of a thrusting spear, Noble Sword (+2 pts), shield (+2 pts), lamellar armour instead of light armour (+2 pts), horse (free; Movement 8"). The horse may have barding (+4 pts). Army General. Fearsome. If mounted on a horse, counts as Steppe Nomad Cavalry. 0-1. (The Art of War p.70)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="f64b-40ce-1981-4d9f" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">6+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
